  [
    '**`heartbeat(id, token, { leaseMs })`** returns `{ leaseUntil }`. Throws `StaleLeaseError` if the lease is no longer yours.',
    '**`heartbeat(id, token, { leaseMs })`** returns `{ leaseUntil }`. Throws `StaleLeaseError` if the lease is no longer yours. The new deadline is written to the log, so every process, including whichever one runs the reaper, sees it.',
  ],
  [
    '**`complete(id, token, result)`** records the result. Throws `StaleLeaseError` if the lease is no longer yours. RFC 007 changes what this returns.',
    "**`complete(id, token, result)`** commits the result and returns a receipt `{ id, outcome, token, result, completedAt, completionSeq }`. `outcome` is `'committed'` the first time. A repeat with the token that committed, even after a restart or a compaction, returns the stored receipt with `outcome: 'already-committed'` and writes nothing. Any other token throws `StaleLeaseError`; a pruned job throws `UnknownJobError`. A lease past its deadline can still commit until a reaper, a reclaim, a cancel or a new claim has acted on it. See [rfc-007-exactly-once-completion.md](rfc-007-exactly-once-completion.md).",
  ],
  [
    '**`reapExpired()`** returns jobs whose lease had run out to the queue, and returns `[{ id, status, retryAt }]`.',
    "**`reapExpired()`** returns jobs whose lease had run out to the queue, and returns `[{ id, status, retryAt }]`.\n\n**`reclaimWorker(workerId, { reason })`** gives up every lease held by a worker that is known to be dead, at once, and returns `[{ id, status }]`. Jobs come back `ready` with no backoff, or `dead` if their attempts have run out; the attempt counts and `reason` becomes `lastError`. Jobs the worker already committed are not touched.\n\n**`getResult(id)`** returns `{ id, status: 'done', result, token, attempts, completedAt, completionSeq }` for a finished job, `{ id, status }` for any other job, and `null` for a job that is not known (never existed, or pruned). **`completions({ after = 0, limit })`** returns the retained commits in commit order, `[{ seq, id, token, result, completedAt }]`, with `seq > after`. Numbers start at 1 and carry on across restarts and compaction.",
  ],
  [
    '`attempts`, `fence` (the current token), `maxAttempts`',
    '`attempts`, `fence` (the current token; it only goes up and is never reused for a job), `maxAttempts`',
  ],
  ['`completedAt`, `seq`.', '`completedAt`, `completionSeq`, `seq`.'],
  [
    '- `start()` starts the workers.',
    "- `start()` starts the workers. Worker ids are unique to the pool (`<pool>-w<n>`), so pools sharing a queue directory never touch each other's jobs.",
  ],
  [
    'The pool is an `EventEmitter`.',
    'When a worker exits, the pool calls `reclaimWorker()` for it straight away, so its jobs do not wait for their leases, and then starts a replacement. A worker that has run a handler keeps trying to record the outcome until it is recorded or the job turns out to belong to someone else (`job-fenced`), and takes no other job meanwhile.\n\nThe pool is an `EventEmitter`.',
  ],
]);

