    '# Changelog\n\n## 0.5.0\n\nCrash and concurrency fixes, and RFC 007.\n\n- Recovery: an incomplete tail is cut off before the next write, so a crash during an append no longer makes a later start fail. The header of a new log and the temp file of a compaction are synced before they take their names.\n- Records and logs of any size up to the format limit work. A catch-up reads the whole log, not its first megabyte.\n- Claims, the reaper and idempotency keys decide under the lock. Tokens are checked, and never reused.\n- Heartbeats and completions are written and synced, so a live worker keeps its job and a completion survives a power cut.\n- Retry due times, attempts, fences, priorities and idempotency keys survive restarts and compaction.\n- Compaction clears a stale temp file, tells processes apart by generation, and rewrites in proportion to what is written. `walq tail` no longer holds the log open.\n- RFC 007: `complete()` returns a receipt; `getResult()`, `completions()` and `reclaimWorker()`; the `release` record; pools reclaim a worker that exits; workers keep trying to record a finished job.\n',
